---
import Legal from '../../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site } from '../../lib/site';

/** The privacy policy in English (`/en/privacidad`). */
const { legal } = site;
---

<Legal title="Privacy policy">
  <p>
    This policy explains what personal data we collect through this website and what we do with it,
    under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and Spanish Organic Law 3/2018 (LOPDGDD).
  </p>

  <h2>Controller</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      {legal.owner} (Tax ID {legal.taxId})
    </li>
    <li>{legal.address}</li>
    <li>
      <a href={`mailto:${legal.email}`}>{legal.email}</a>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What data we collect and why</h2>
  <p>
    Only what you give us when you write to us (through the form, by email or by WhatsApp): your
    name, your email, your phone if you add it and your message. We use it only to answer you and,
    if we reach an agreement, to provide the service. We do not use it to send you advertising.
  </p>

  <h2>Legal basis</h2>
  <p>
    Your consent when you send us the message (article 6.1.a GDPR) and, when you ask us for a quote
    or an appointment, steps taken at your request before a contract (article 6.1.b).
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    As long as needed to deal with your enquiry. Messages sent through the form are kept for 12
    months at most and then deleted. If you become a customer, for as long as the relationship lasts
    and the periods the law requires (for example, tax rules).
  </p>

  <h2>Who else can access it</h2>
  <p>
    We do not share your data with anyone, unless the law requires it. Our website and form hosting
    provider accesses it only to provide that service to us, as a processor: it sends us your
    messages by email and keeps them in our private area so that we can read them, and uses them for
    nothing else. If you write to us on WhatsApp, that service belongs to WhatsApp Ireland Limited
    and follows its own policy.
  </p>

  {site.analytics ? (
    <>
      <h2>Visit statistics</h2>
      <p>
        We count visits to the website in aggregate (pages viewed, where visitors come from, the
        type of device) with our own tool, which uses no cookies and does not keep your IP address.
        It cannot identify you.
      </p>
    </>
  ) : null}

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask us to access, correct or delete your data, to object to or restrict its processing,
    or to take it with you, by writing to <a href={`mailto:${legal.email}`}>{legal.email}</a>. If
    you think we have not handled it properly, you can complain to the Spanish Data Protection
    Agency (
    <a href="https://www.aepd.es" rel="noopener" target="_blank">
      www.aepd.es
    </a>
    ).
  </p>
</Legal>
